From 3fb1d2afbbab0e8b7624c6b4955dd6e335bde8d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:44:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a fullscreen control and fix mobile/tablet visibility
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The play/pause + mute bar only ever revealed on :hover, so it never
appeared on touch devices — there's no hover there. It's now always
visible on any pointer without a mouse (pointer-fine decides, not a
screen-width breakpoint, since a touch laptop or a stylus doesn't
split neatly along one), and still hover-reveals on an actual mouse.

Adds a third button, fullscreen, next to play/pause and mute. It
fullscreens the video's own wrapper rather than the bare video, so
this same control bar stays on screen once fullscreen, with one
exception: iOS Safari never implemented the standard Fullscreen API
on anything but the video element, so it falls back to the native
player there.
